"""Definitions and distinct needs, in the words the business uses (definition standard, references/definitions.md)."""
from __future__ import annotations

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- concepts: (definition, distinct need)
CONCEPTS: dict[str, tuple[str, str]] = {
    "SBJ001": ("There is one of these for each person the business deals with, such as an operator, a technician or a supplier's contact. If you need to know who someone is, this is what you go by. What they do for the business is held beside it, and who employs them comes from the relationship with their employer.", ""),
    "SBJ002": ("There is one of these for each qualification a person holds to carry out particular work, such as running a filling line or taking a sample. If you need to know whether someone was qualified to do a job on a given day, this is what you go by. It does not record the work they actually did, which is recorded against the batch.",
               "Holds what a person is qualified to do and for how long; nothing else says whether they were entitled to do a piece of work."),
    "SBJ003": ("There is one of these for each shift a person is rostered to work. If you need to know who was on duty at a given time, this is what you go by. It does not say what they worked on, which is recorded against each production run, and it does not say whether they were qualified for it.",
               "Holds who was on duty and when; no other record says who was present."),
    "SBJ004": ("There is one of these for each time a person puts their name to a record, whether to say they did the work or to confirm another person's work as a second check. If you need to know who signed a record, when, and what the signing meant, this is what you go by. A correction to a record is a record of its own and is not a signing.",
               "Holds who signed what, when and with what meaning; nothing else shows the signing."),
    "SBJ005": ("There is one of these for each company, partnership or other body that can hold rights and owe duties in its own name, such as a supplier, an outside manufacturer, a customer or a regulator. If you need to know who a body is, this is what you go by. What it is to the business comes from its relationships and is not stored here.", ""),
    "SBJ006": ("There is one of these for each identifier a legal entity is known by, such as a registration number, a tax number or a number a regulator issued. If you need to match a supplier or an outside manufacturer to a register, this is what you go by. It does not say which identifier is preferred.", ""),
    "SBJ007": ("There is one of these for each address a legal entity is known by, such as its registered office or the address it writes from. If you need to know where to write to a body, this is what you go by. It is not the place where the body makes or stores goods, which is a place held with Locations.", ""),
    "SBJ008": ("There is one of these for each time a supplier or an outside manufacturer is assessed, saying what the assessment covered and how long it is valid. If you need to know whether a supplier held a valid assessment on the day a delivery arrived, this is what you go by. The problems raised against the supplier are not held here; each is recorded as a finding.",
               "Holds each assessment of a supplier and how long it lasts; no other record says whether a supplier was assessed."),
    "SBJ009": ("There is one of these for each request the business makes to a supplier to put a problem right, with the supplier's answer. If you need to know what a supplier was asked to do and how they replied, this is what you go by. The action the business takes itself is not held here; it is recorded as a corrective action.",
               "Holds what a supplier was asked and how they answered; the business's own actions are held as corrective actions."),
    "SBJ010": ("There is one of these for each document the business keeps, such as a supplier's certificate, a test report or a method statement. If you need to find a document and know what kind it is, this is what you go by. What the document says about a batch is held as its declarations.", ""),
    "SBJ011": ("There is one of these for each property a supplier's document states about a batch, such as a moisture level or the absence of an allergen. If you need to know what a supplier claims about a batch, and so what the business relies on without having tested it, this is what you go by. A test the business carried out itself is a test result and is not held here.",
               "Holds what a supplier claims about a batch; no other record separates a claim from the business's own result."),
    "SBJ012": ("There is one of these for each product the organisation makes, buys or sells that is a physical thing, such as a raw material, a pack component, an intermediate or a finished product. If you need to know which product a batch is of, and whether it is bought in or made, this is what you go by. What the product is made from, what it must be and what its pack says are held by CPG - Product Definition.",
               "Anchors the products the manufacturing records refer to; what a product is, is held by CPG - Product Definition."),
    "SBJ016": ("There is one of these for each batch of a product that was made, packed or received, known by the lot code given when it was first packed or transformed. If you need to know when it was made, how much there was and what to call it at every later movement, this is what you go by. What went into it and where it went are held on the links between production runs and batches.",
               "Holds each batch and its lot code; nothing else identifies the quantity that traceability follows."),
    "SBJ017": ("There is one of these for each part a batch is divided into, with the quantity of that part. If you need to know which batch a quantity came from, this is what you go by. A batch combined from others is shown by the links between production runs and batches, not here.",
               "Holds each part a batch was divided into; without it a quantity can appear with no batch to come from."),
    "SBJ026": ("There is one of these for each machine, vessel or tool, and for each individually identified unit of product, that is tracked on its own. If you need to know which machine stood in a place or what is inside a unit, this is what you go by. A kind of machine, or a product, which many of them share, is not held here.",
               "Holds each machine and each individually identified unit as itself; products and batches hold what is shared."),
    "SBJ027": ("There is one of these for each identifier a machine or unit is known by, such as a serial number or an asset number, with the dates it applied. If you need to match a machine to its maker's records, this is what you go by. It does not say which identifier is preferred.",
               "Holds the identifiers a machine or unit is known by and who issued them; no other record holds an identifier of a machine."),
    "SBJ028": ("There is one of these for each reading taken of a machine's condition, such as a temperature or the hours it has run, with the time it was taken. If you need to know how a machine was running before it failed, this is what you go by. A failure itself is recorded as a stoppage.",
               "Holds the readings taken of a machine; nothing else shows its condition over time."),
    "SBJ029": ("There is one of these for each way a machine is known to fail, with what the failure does. If you need to know how a machine fails and what follows when it does, this is what you go by. A particular breakdown is recorded as a stoppage, not here.",
               "Holds each known way a machine fails; a breakdown that happened is held as a stoppage."),
    "SBJ034": ("There is one of these for each rule about what may run on a line straight after what, with the reason and whether a clean is needed between. If you need to know whether one product may follow another on a line, this is what you go by. What actually ran, and whether the clean was done, is recorded as changeovers.",
               "Holds the rules for what may follow what on a line; what happened is held as changeovers."),
    "SBJ036": ("There is one of these for each defined step of work in making a product, such as mixing, pasteurising or filling. If you need to know what a step is called and what it does, this is what you go by. The order steps run in belongs to the method, and the performing of a step is recorded against the batch.", "Holds each defined step of work; the method holds the order and the batch holds the performing."),
    "SBJ037": ("There is one of these for each thing a step needs, whether a kind of machine, a qualified person or a material. If you need to know what must be in place before a step can run, this is what you go by. It does not say which machine or person was used on a given day, which is recorded against the production run.",
               "Holds what each step needs; no other record says what must be in place before a step runs."),
    "SBJ038": ("There is one of these for each setting a step is run at, such as a temperature or a speed, with the lowest and highest value allowed. If you need to know the limits a step must stay within, this is what you go by. The value used for a given batch is held with the recipe instructions.",
               "Holds the limits for each setting of a step; the values used are held with the recipe."),
    "SBJ039": ("There is one of these for each plan for taking samples at a step, saying how often. If you need to know how often a step is sampled, this is what you go by. The sample actually taken and its result are recorded as a test.",
               "Holds how often each step is sampled; the samples taken are held as tests."),
    "SBJ040": ("There is one of these for each method by which a product is made, as an ordered set of steps. If you need to know how a product is made and in what order, this is what you go by. The steps themselves are held separately, and the making of a batch is recorded as a production run.",
               "Holds each method of making a product; the steps and the runs are held separately."),
    "SBJ041": ("There is one of these for each level a recipe is written at, from the general recipe the company holds, through the site recipe and the master recipe, to the instructions issued for one batch. If you need to know which instructions a batch was made to and where they came from, this is what you go by. What the product is made from is held by CPG - Product Definition.",
               "Holds the four levels of each recipe and which each came from; nothing else says which instructions a batch was made to."),
    "SBJ042": ("There is one of these for each value a setting is given at a particular level of a recipe. If you need to know what a setting was set to for a batch, this is what you go by. The limits the setting must stay within are held with the setting itself.",
               "Holds the value each setting took at each recipe level; the limits are held with the setting."),
    "SBJ043": ("There is one of these for each place the organisation needs to identify, from a site down through its areas, lines, rooms and storage positions to the shop floor, and each site a supplier, an outside manufacturer or a customer works from. If you need to know where something was made, held or sent, this is what you go by. Who owns or runs the place comes from its relationship with a legal entity, and the machines standing in it are held with Instances.",
               "Holds every place from the site to the shop floor in one hierarchy; no other concept names a place."),
    "SBJ044": ("There is one of these for each identifier a place is known by, such as a site number or a registration number a regulator issued, with who issued it. If you need to match a place to a supplier's or a regulator's record, this is what you go by. It does not say which identifier is preferred.",
               "Holds the identifiers of a place and who issued each; no other record holds them."),
    "SBJ045": ("There is one of these for each condition a place must keep stock in, such as a temperature range. If you need to know what a storage place must hold to, this is what you go by. A time the condition was broken is recorded as a storage breach.",
               "Holds the conditions each place must keep; breaches of them are held as events."),
    "SBJ046": ("There is one of these for each time goods are received, issued, moved, bought or despatched, with the time it happened. If you need to know where goods went and when, this is what you go by. How much of an item is held at a point in time is held as stock positions.",
               "Holds each movement of goods; stock held is a separate count."),
    "SBJ047": ("There is one of these for each item and quantity on a movement of goods. If you need to know how much of what moved, this is what you go by. The parties and places of the movement are held on the movement itself.",
               "Holds the quantity of each item on a movement; the movement holds the parties and places."),
    "SBJ048": ("There is one of these for each count of an item held at a place, in a stated condition, at a time. If you need to know how much is available, on hold or rejected right now, this is what you go by. A decision to hold material is recorded as a disposition.",
               "Holds how much is held, in what condition and where, as at a time; movements show how it got there."),
    "SBJ049": ("There is one of these for each thing that happens in making or handling goods that the business needs to record, with the time it happened. If you need to know that something happened and when, this is what you go by. What kind of thing it was, and its details, are held by the concept for that kind.", "Anchors everything that happens and when; each concept for a kind of event holds the details of that kind."),
    "SBJ051": ("There is one of these for each time a batch is made on a line, from its start to its end. If you need to know what was made, where, when and how much of each input was used, this is what you go by. The instructions it was made to are held as recipe levels, and the batch itself is held with the product.",
               "Holds each making of a batch; the inputs used and the outputs produced are held on its links to batches."),
    "SBJ053": ("There is one of these for each time a batch is divided into parts, with the reason. If you need to know why a batch was divided, this is what you go by. The parts and their quantities are held as sub-batches.",
               "Holds why a batch was divided; the parts are held as sub-batches."),
    "SBJ054": ("There is one of these for each time a line is switched from one product to another, with how long it took and whether it included a clean. If you need to know whether a line was cleaned between two products, this is what you go by. The rule about what may follow what is held as a sequencing rule.",
               "Holds each changeover and whether it included a clean; the rule it was held to is a sequencing rule."),
    "SBJ055": ("There is one of these for each time production stops, with when it started, when it ended and why. If you need to know how long a line stopped and for what reason, this is what you go by. The repair that followed is recorded as maintenance work.",
               "Holds each stoppage once, with its reason; the repair is tied to it as maintenance work."),
    "SBJ056": ("There is one of these for each piece of maintenance or repair work done on a machine, saying what was done. If you need to know what was done about a stoppage, this is what you go by. The stoppage itself is held as a stoppage, and the machine's wider history is held on the machine.",
               "Holds the work done on a machine; the stoppage it answers is held separately."),
    "SBJ057": ("There is one of these for each test of a sample, with the method, the result, whether it met the specification and which version of the specification it was judged against. If you need to know whether a batch met its specification and by what test, this is what you go by. The specification itself is held by CPG - Product Definition.",
               "Holds each test and the version of the specification it was judged against; the specification is held by CPG - Product Definition."),
    "SBJ058": ("There is one of these for each departure from procedure or failure against specification that is found, saying which it is, how serious it is and how it was contained. If you need to know what went wrong on a batch, this is what you go by. What was decided about the affected material is recorded as a disposition.",
               "Holds each departure from procedure and each failure against specification, kept apart by kind; nothing else says what went wrong."),
    "SBJ060": ("There is one of these for each decision about what is done with material that failed, such as rework or scrap, with the reason. If you need to know what was decided about failed material and why, this is what you go by. The failure itself is recorded as a finding.",
               "Holds each decision about failed material and its reason; the failure is held as a finding."),
    "SBJ061": ("There is one of these for each action taken to put right the cause of a problem, with the cause found, the check that the fix worked and when it was closed. If you need to know whether an action was closed before anyone checked it worked, this is what you go by. The problem itself is recorded as a finding.",
               "Holds each corrective action, its cause and its check; no other record shows whether an action was verified."),
    "SBJ062": ("There is one of these for each time a batch is released for use or sale, with who released it, when and on what basis. If you need to know whether and why a batch was released, this is what you go by. A batch that has finished being made is not available until this exists.",
               "Holds each release of a batch and its basis; a batch that has finished is not released until this exists."),
    "SBJ063": ("There is one of these for each recall of product already sent out, with what it covered. If you need to know what was recalled and why, this is what you go by. The batches a recall reached are found through the links between batches, not here.",
               "Holds each recall and what it covered; the batches reached come from the traced links."),
    "SBJ064": ("There is one of these for each complaint received about a product, with the report as it was given. If you need to know what a customer reported and which batch it was about, this is what you go by. The investigation that follows is recorded as findings and corrective actions.",
               "Holds each complaint as reported; the investigation is held as findings and actions."),
    "SBJ065": ("There is one of these for each correction made to an earlier record, saying why. If you need to know that a record was altered and why, this is what you go by. The earlier record is kept as it was and is never overwritten.",
               "Holds each correction and its reason; without it an alteration could go unrecorded."),
    "SBJ066": ("There is one of these for each time stock was held outside the conditions its place must keep, with when it began. If you need to know whether a batch was ever stored out of condition, this is what you go by. The conditions themselves are held with the place.",
               "Holds each time stock was held out of condition; the conditions are held with the place."),
    "SBJ067": ("There is one of these for each level a product is packed in, such as a single unit, a case or a pallet, with how many of the level below it holds. If you need to know how many units are in a case and how many cases are on a pallet, this is what you go by. What is in the pack and the wording on it are held by CPG - Product Definition.",
               "Holds the levels a product is packed in and how many of the level below each holds; nothing else in the model holds pack levels."),
}

